      "apiDescription": "## Props\n\n```\nexport type GIconButtonProps = {\n  /**\n   * disable the button\n   *\n   * @default false\n   */\n  disabled?: boolean;\n  /**\n   * Specifies that a button should automatically get focus when the page loads.\n   *\n   * Only if the `href` is disabled.\n   *\n   * @default false\n   */\n  autofocus?: boolean;\n  /**\n   * If you write an href the component behaves with an `a`.\n   * Specifies the URL of the page the link goes to\n   *\n   * @default undefined\n   */\n  href?: string;\n  /**\n   * Specifies where to open the linked document.\n   *\n   * Only if the `href` is active\n   *\n   * @default undefined\n   */\n  target?: string;\n  /**\n   * Specifies that the target will be downloaded when a user clicks on the hyperlink.\n   *\n   * Only if the href is active.\n   *\n   * @default undefined\n   */\n  download?: string;\n  /**\n   * button variant `grey / black / blue`\n   *\n   * @default 'grey'\n   */\n  variant?: IconButtonVariant;\n  /**\n   * Left icon rendered using the IconFont component.\n   *\n   * The icon should be specified using the format \"<weight> <icon-name>\".\n   * Acceptable weights are: \"solid\", \"regular\", \"light\", \"brands\", or \"duotone\".\n   *\n   * @see IconFont documentation for available icons.\n   * @example 'solid check', 'regular user'\n   * @default 'solid check'\n   */\n  icon?: IconString;\n  /**\n   * Acceptable sizes are: \"medium\" or \"small\".\n   *\n   * @default 'medium'\n   */\n  size?: IconButtonSize;\n  /** @default false */\n  border?: boolean;\n  /** @default false */\n  rounded?: boolean;\n  /**\n   * Specifies the type of button (only when not using href).\n   * Allowed values are: \"button\", \"submit\", \"reset\".\n   *\n   * @default 'button'\n   */\n  type?: \"button\" | \"submit\" | \"reset\";\n}\n```\n\n## Events\n\n```\nexport type GIconButtonEvents = {\n  click: [evt: MouseEvent];\n  mousedown: [evt: MouseEvent];\n}\n```",
